            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic activity of dimeric proanthocyanidins--Preliminary experiments.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>145-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pharmacological experiments with cacao and avocado proanthocyanidins were performed. Analgesic action was measured by the heated plate method: mice receiving 80mg/kg of the drugs showed a behaviour similar to those receiving morphine. Potentiation of &quot;sleeping time&quot; suggests a possible depressive action on the central nervous system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
